{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a9768d65-a49e-4aaf-a8a1-3112cf722565","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-acbf2b60df8f4989","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-gx63tfdy/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E001.md","content":"# PQC Readiness Matrix and compliance tracking for all RHOAI runtime images\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the central coordination artifact of the PQC base image compliance\neffort for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0: a per-component PQC Readiness Matrix covering every RHOAI\nruntime image (starting from the RHOAI 3.5 payload inventory of 153 relatedImages in\nRHOAI-Build-Config and the organized local image inventory), plus the tracking process\nthat gives OCP 5.0 an aggregated compliance view. The strategy names this design doc as\n\"to be created — PQC Readiness Matrix per component\". Each component team owns its own\nbase-image switch or OCP exception filing; this epic provides the inventory, target\nmapping, status ledger, and deadline enforcement that make their status visible and the\nSeptember 15, 2026 deadline enforceable.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build the PQC Readiness Matrix from the RHOAI 3.5 relatedImages inventory\n  (RHOAI-Build-Config rhoai-3.5 CSV) and the organized image inventory, with one row per\n  RHOAI runtime image:\n  - current base image (per the strategy's base image mapping: `ubi9/ubi-minimal`,\n    `rhel9-6-els/rhel:9.6-*`, `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`,\n    `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, `ubi9/nodejs-22`, `ubi9/openjdk-17-runtime`)\n  - target PQC base image (`ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, PQC variant\n    TBD for python/nodejs bases, or OCP exception)\n  - TLS stack classification (system OpenSSL / rustls+ring / Java-NSS) determining\n    whether a base image swap can remediate the component\n  - owning team and linked tracking ticket\n  - status: switched / exception-filed / in-progress / unassigned, with delivery tier\n    (Tier 1 confirmed bases vs. Tier 2 dependency-gated bases)\n- Encode the runtime-only switch guidance: only the final runtime stage of each\n  Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is needed.\n- Stand up the compliance tracking process: component team tracking tickets linked to\n  RHAISTRAT-8001 for aggregated OCP 5.0 visibility, an exception ledger (filed and\n  acknowledged OCP exceptions with documented remediation plans), weekly reminders to\n  teams, and the escalation path to leadership agreed in the Mara/Devin sync for teams\n  that risk missing September 15 without an exception on file.\n- Track the external dependency posture in the matrix: PQC variants of\n  `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/nodejs-22` (RHOAIENG-7195 with AIPCC) and\n  the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) gating `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` adoption,\n  escalating per the strategy if no committed date by early September.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the RHOAI 3.5 relatedImages inventory, when the readiness matrix is reviewed,\n  then every one of the ~153 runtime images has a row with current base, target base or\n  exception intent, TLS stack classification, owning team, and status — zero images\n  missing from the matrix.\n- Every component team's tracking ticket that exists is linked to RHAISTRAT-8001, and\n  teams without a linked ticket have been reminded at least weekly, with escalation\n  raised to leadership for any team still unresponsive after two consecutive reminders.\n- The exception ledger records, for each filed OCP exception, the component, its TLS\n  stack, the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, and its remediation plan.\n- The matrix documents, per image, whether only the final runtime stage changes\n  (runtime-only enablement) and which images are gated on unconfirmed dependencies\n  (python/nodejs PQC variants, RHEL 9.8 rebase) versus available now.\n- The escalation criteria from the strategy (no committed AIPCC date by early September)\n  are documented in the tracking process and have been applied or found not applicable.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image for RHOAI 3.6 /\n  OCP 5.0** — this epic produces the per-image target mapping and switch-status tracking\n  that aggregate each team's compliance work.\n- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception with a\n  remediation plan** — this epic owns the exception ledger, deadline reminders, and\n  escalation process.\n- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of the\n  Dockerfile/Containerfile changes** — this epic encodes the runtime-stage-only switch\n  guidance in the matrix instructions given to every team.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38050,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2ed9b966d085149","agent_id":"adb5edffc4ae3a249","session_id":"516e0302-0205-40f2-ace9-cb4df5d195a7","uuid":"707bfd1e-9e8c-4d44-87eb-8f65ea28a3e6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:51:52.639Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
