{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a9768d65-a49e-4aaf-a8a1-3112cf722565","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aca20f0998261cfb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-gx63tfdy/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E003.md","content":"# Payload-wide PQC base image compliance verification and final accounting\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the release-gating verification for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0 PQC\ncompliance: an automated scan across the RHOAI 3.6 payload proving that switched runtime\nimages activate the `DEFAULT:PQ` crypto policy with ML-KEM algorithms available, and the\nfinal compliance accounting showing that every RHOAI component image is either rebuilt on\na PQC-enabled base image or covered by a filed and acknowledged OCP exception — zero\nunaccounted-for images. The verification runs against the image inventory and exception\nledger maintained by the readiness matrix and compliance tracking work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement or wire up the payload-wide compliance scan that executes\n  `update-crypto-policies --show` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` inside the runtime\n  containers of the RHOAI 3.6 payload and records the results per image. The companion\n  strategy RHAISTRAT-7816 owns TLS-scanner CI; if its scanner covers the crypto-policy\n  check, integrate it — otherwise implement a dedicated crypto-policy scan (boundary to\n  be confirmed, see decomposition health warnings).\n- Apply the scan's applicability rules from the strategy: OpenSSL-backed components only\n  (Go operators, Python components, native-tls Rust components); components on\n  non-OpenSSL TLS stacks (rustls+ring, Java/NSS) are covered by OCP exception filings,\n  not by the scan; on FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivates PQC for this release —\n  `DEFAULT:PQ` being inactive there is expected and is not a compliance failure.\n- Produce the final compliance accounting for the September 15, 2026 deadline: for every\n  image in the payload inventory, either (a) scan evidence of `DEFAULT:PQ` with\n  ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 present, or (b) a filed and acknowledged OCP\n  exception with a remediation plan naming the component's TLS stack and why it cannot\n  negotiate ML-KEM. The accounting terminates with zero unaccounted-for images.\n- Report residual gaps (images neither switched nor exception-covered) with owning teams\n  for escalation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a switched OpenSSL-backed runtime image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload, when\n  `update-crypto-policies --show` is executed inside the container, then the active\n  crypto policy reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, and when `openssl list -kem-algorithms` is\n  executed, then ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 appear in the output —\n  verified by the automated scan across the payload, with results recorded per image.\n- The scan correctly excludes non-OpenSSL components (covered by exception filings) and\n  treats FIPS-mode clusters as expected-behavior rather than compliance failure, per the\n  strategy's acceptance criteria notes.\n- Given the payload inventory and the exception ledger, when the final accounting is\n  compiled, then every RHOAI component image is in exactly one of two states — scanned\n  PQC-compliant, or covered by a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with remediation\n  plan — and the count of unaccounted-for images is zero, with any residual gaps\n  escalated with named owning teams.\n- The accounting is reproducible: re-running the scan and accounting on the same payload\n  produces the same verdict per image.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image for RHOAI 3.6 /\n  OCP 5.0** — this epic verifies the end state across the payload (strategy Acceptance\n  Criterion 1).\n- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception with a\n  remediation plan** — this epic produces the final switch-vs-exception accounting with\n  zero unaccounted-for images (strategy Acceptance Criterion 2).\n- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only** — the scan targets the runtime container's\n  active crypto policy, validating the runtime-only enablement model end to end.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38050,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2ed9b966d085149","agent_id":"adb5edffc4ae3a249","session_id":"516e0302-0205-40f2-ace9-cb4df5d195a7","uuid":"42dad93b-1c1d-4df8-b33d-c79b203019b7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:52:16.179Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
