coring): E002's scope says \"representative\n64\tPQC-switched images\" without naming the selection source; identifying switched images is\n65\tmost naturally done via E001's status matrix, and the parallel placement would be cleaner\n66\tif the selection source (strategy's base-image mapping table vs. E001's matrix) were\n67\tstated. This does not rise to a missing artifact dependency — E002 can select from the\n68\tstrategy's published inventory independently.\n69\t\n70\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n71\tComponent/team tuples are distinct per epic: E001 (Build and Release / DevOps/Build),\n72\tE002 (PerfScale / Performance), E003 (CI/CD / DevOps/Build) — all three component names\n73\tare in the canonical component list. E001 and E003 share a team but differ in component\n74\tand work surface (tracking artifact vs. automated verification), which the boundary rules\n75\tpermit. No scope duplication: E001 builds the reported-status matrix and exception ledger;\n76\tE003 produces scan evidence and the evidence-based final accounting that consumes E001's\n77\tledger — complementary deliverables the strategy itself distinguishes (tracking\n78\tvisibility vs. AC-1/AC-2 verification), not two epics rebuilding the same surface. No\n79\twork-product type mixing: all three epics produce engineering/tracking artifacts; no epic\n80\tbundles code with sample-notebook or tutorial content. Epic sizes are within a sprint for\n81\tan S-effort coordination strategy. No epic exceeds ~2 weeks.\n82\t\n83\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n84\tAll three epics are typed Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact (E001:\n85\treadiness matrix + exception ledger + tracking process; E002: ratified threshold +\n86\tbenchmark report; E003: automated scan + final accounting). No Investigation epics are\n87\tpresent, and the Unknowns Evaluation correctly justifies this: each open question either\n88\tresolves outside this strategy's epic set (RHOAIENG-7195, AIPCC-7258 — third parties\n89\tresolve, Rule 21 preconditions) or does not change which epics exist (exception-vs-switch\n90\tis tracked subject matter; the threshold value does not alter E002's work). E002 is\n91\tcorrectly Implementation, not Investigation — it produces a measurement report artifact;\n92\tthe threshold ratification is a named human decision the epic drives, not a structure-\n93\tchanging unknown. All `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are null and no epic lists\n94\tan Investigation dependency, so no gating metadata issues exist.\n95\t\n96\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n97\tAll three epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric) with\n98\t`investigation_signals: null` — correct field usage. Rationale files exist for all three\n99\tepics and their tables match the frontmatter values exactly. Signal values are consistent\n100\twith strategy content: E001's `open_questions: 1` is justified (the strategy's open\n101\tquestions are tracked subject matter, not design inputs to the matrix); E002's\n102\t`open_questions: -1` and `human_process_gates: -1` correctly reflect the NEEDS DOMAIN\n103\tINPUT threshold pending PM + Performance lead ratification, and `change_specificity: 0`\n104\tcorrectly reflects the undefined numeric threshold/methodology; E003's\n105\t`pattern_precedent: 0` is justified given the unconfirmed RHAISTRAT-7816 scanner boundary.\n106\tNo signal value contradicts the rubric conditions. (Arithmetic and thresholds not checked,\n107\tper review rules — computed by pipeline.)\n108\t\n109\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n110\tEvery epic has testable, strategy-derived ACs. E001's ACs are countable and verifiable\n111\t(~153 rows with required fields, tickets linked, ledger contents, escalation criteria\n112\tapplied). E002's ACs are verifiable (ratified threshold document, per-class pass/fail\n113\tverdicts, report delivered with named remediation owners). E003's ACs directly restate the\n114\tstrategy's AC-1/AC-2 in